<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamad bin Thuwaini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamad bin Thuwaini was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Zanzibar from 1893 to 1896, ruling under the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. A grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-sultan">Said bin Sultan</a> through Thuwaini, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a>, he was chosen with British approval. His sudden death on 25 August 1896 led his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-bin-barghash">Khalid bin Barghash</a> to seize the palace, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zanzibar-war">Anglo-Zanzibar War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamad-bin-thuwaini.jpg" alt="Hamad bin Thuwaini" width="180" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamad_bin_Thwiny_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
